WEBVTT

00:02.750 --> 00:03.920
Karinpani.

00:04.420 --> 00:08.080
When the Ezo mountain sakura 
flowers bloom, the deer grow new coats,

00:08.080 --> 00:10.330
and it's said to be a sign that 
their meat will taste better.

00:10.770 --> 00:13.370
That's a good sign!

00:13.370 --> 00:16.600
You wrap the bark of the cherry blossom 
trees around your bow to make it stronger,

00:16.600 --> 00:17.370
so it won't break.

00:17.910 --> 00:20.120
You also wrap it around your 
makiri and your quiver.

00:20.120 --> 00:23.410
You also use it to bind the boards 
of your itaomacip together.

00:23.410 --> 00:26.450
So it's an important tree for hunting.

00:26.450 --> 00:30.030
That tree you call a 
mayumi, we call a kasupni,

00:30.030 --> 00:31.760
which means "ladle tree".

00:32.220 --> 00:35.890
Its wood is hard and fine-grained, 
so we use it for ladles and spatulas.

00:36.550 --> 00:38.760
We also use it for a ceremonial arrow

00:38.760 --> 00:41.830
called a heperay that we 
use for the bear rituals,

00:41.830 --> 00:44.390
and for the kite we use to 
hunt large sea creatures.

00:44.980 --> 00:49.070
These arrows are said to lead the 
baby bear to where the kamuy dwell.

00:49.070 --> 00:51.360
That's an important tree.

00:49.170 --> 00:53.030
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:53.670 --> 00:58.510
<b>Episode Forty-Nine
The Vanished Kamuy</b>

00:57.940 --> 01:00.630
Hey Usami, dial it back a bit.

01:00.630 --> 01:02.040
Your dick's gonna catch fire.

01:02.040 --> 01:05.750
It's our one way to solve 
the case, and it's working!

01:05.750 --> 01:07.230
Shut up!

01:07.850 --> 01:11.760
Out of the rest of the 7th Division, 
Ogata was a pretty big weirdo too, but...

01:11.760 --> 01:14.090
Don't compare me to him!

01:14.090 --> 01:16.640
He's just a wimpy, snot-nosed kid!

01:16.640 --> 01:17.760
Fuck!

01:18.800 --> 01:22.250
Do you remember Lieutenant Hanazawa?

01:22.250 --> 01:26.330
Ogata's half-brother, who died 
at the Battle of Hill 203?

01:26.330 --> 01:27.560
Fuck!

01:30.190 --> 01:31.960
Of course I do.

01:31.960 --> 01:33.980
Well, get this.

01:34.560 --> 01:37.340
When Sugimoto threw Ogata into 
a freezing river in winter,

01:37.340 --> 01:38.990
and he was in the hospital...

01:44.430 --> 01:47.400
Yuusaku-dono...

01:50.800 --> 01:52.590
Yuusaku-dono?

01:53.300 --> 01:57.090
He was calling out the name of 
the little brother he killed!

01:57.690 --> 02:00.760
Ogata killed Lieutenant Hanazawa?

02:00.760 --> 02:03.100
Oh, you didn't know?

02:04.330 --> 02:05.560
Why?

02:06.150 --> 02:07.920
They seemed to get along.

02:10.580 --> 02:12.770
<b>Russo-Japanese War   The Siege of Port Arthur</b>

02:13.060 --> 02:16.690
Lieutenant Tsurumi says not to kill him?

02:18.050 --> 02:22.560
But if Yuusaku-dono dies, then
you will get all his father's love,

02:22.560 --> 02:26.260
and he'll be able to control 
Lieutenant General Hanazawa.

02:26.260 --> 02:27.960
That sucks.

02:29.230 --> 02:32.740
He must've decided that Yuusaku-dono 
would serve as a tool,

02:32.740 --> 02:35.050
because of how much everyone worships him.

02:35.050 --> 02:37.740
Only 'cause of who his dad is, right?

02:37.740 --> 02:40.590
They all think he's a better 
person than he is, right?

02:41.110 --> 02:47.810
That's right. Once he sees that, 
Lieutenant Tsurumi will change his mind.

02:48.140 --> 02:50.680
Everybody's all the same beneath the skin.

02:52.400 --> 02:56.680
Hey, you don't regret 
killing Russians, do you?

02:56.680 --> 02:57.820
Nope.

02:58.290 --> 03:01.280
You get killed because you 
deserve it, in some sense.

03:01.280 --> 03:03.030
Yes, I agree.

03:03.790 --> 03:06.620
And everybody has the potential to do wrong.

03:07.030 --> 03:10.610
Killing someone like that shouldn't 
make you feel guilty, right?

03:10.610 --> 03:12.290
Not in the slightest.

03:13.040 --> 03:17.760
Just because your parents love you 
more doesn't make you a better person.

03:17.760 --> 03:19.310
Very true!

03:20.190 --> 03:22.660
So there's nothing wrong with me, then.

03:25.840 --> 03:28.600
I want to see you kill.

03:29.190 --> 03:30.140
I can't!

03:33.370 --> 03:37.480
Looks like you weren't able to 
show everyone who he really is!

03:38.350 --> 03:39.930
Well that's not good.

03:40.420 --> 03:42.750
Maybe I am the weird one?

03:43.300 --> 03:45.930
Is it because I'm the unloved 
child of a mistress?

03:46.710 --> 03:49.250
No, wait.

03:50.320 --> 03:54.570
What if Father actually did love me?

03:54.570 --> 03:59.750
Then there'd be no difference 
between me and Yuusaku-dono.

04:00.910 --> 04:09.680
Which would mean he's no saint. He's got 
the potential to kill without guilt.

04:10.310 --> 04:13.610
So how do I find out if 
Father really loves me?

04:14.320 --> 04:17.150
I just need to get rid of Yuusaku-dono.

04:17.770 --> 04:18.880
Am I right?

04:20.170 --> 04:21.400
Sounds right to me!

04:23.870 --> 04:27.660
And well... it all ended 
up just like we planned!

04:28.080 --> 04:31.880
Would Lieutenant General Hanazawa now 
feel love towards Hyakunosuke,

04:31.880 --> 04:33.410
who he already abandoned once?

04:34.140 --> 04:35.290
The answer was...

04:35.880 --> 04:38.510
Not at all!

04:39.990 --> 04:45.010
He's got permanent blue balls 
'cause Yuusaku-dono died pure!

04:45.010 --> 04:46.680
Isn't that precious?

04:48.460 --> 04:50.130
I've got better things to do.

04:50.130 --> 04:51.980
Neigh-hey!

04:54.090 --> 04:58.360
I know you were egging on the traitors.

05:00.230 --> 05:03.400
What is it about Lieutenant Tsurumi 
that's not good enough for you?

05:05.090 --> 05:07.820
Don't tell me that's why.

05:18.980 --> 05:23.030
He's sure to see in you the 
brave fighter that he lost.

05:23.030 --> 05:25.800
Well done, Ogata Hyakunosuke.

05:36.300 --> 05:39.850
Did you agree to kill Lieutenant 
General Hanazawa because you

05:39.850 --> 05:42.190
thought it would make you 
head of the 7th Division?

05:42.720 --> 05:46.570
No, I just wanted to talk with him 
about some things before he died.

05:46.570 --> 05:48.940
You don't think that if your 
influence in the division gets stronger,

05:48.940 --> 05:53.180
Lieutenant Tsurumi will 
start loving you, right?

05:54.050 --> 05:55.040
Nope.

05:55.270 --> 05:57.850
Look into the Manchurian railroad.

05:57.850 --> 06:01.840
Lieutenant Tsurumi just saw
 your dad as in the way.

06:02.430 --> 06:06.600
You killed Yuusaku-dono, 
but your father won't love you.

06:06.600 --> 06:11.540
You killed your father, 
but Lieutenant Tsurumi won't love you.

06:11.540 --> 06:14.810
Nobody loves you, and it drives you nuts!

06:15.130 --> 06:18.580
And so you're blaming it all 
on Lieutenant Tsurumi, aren't you?

06:19.310 --> 06:24.300
Know your place. We're just
 Lieutenant Tsurumi's pawns.

06:24.300 --> 06:26.440
Learn from Sergeant Tsukishima!

06:26.440 --> 06:29.510
He knows damn well that he's a pawn!

06:30.340 --> 06:35.140
Lieutenant Tsurumi, that was great.
 That was wonderful.

06:35.670 --> 06:37.250
What are you talking about?

06:37.530 --> 06:41.250
You called Sergeant Tsukishima 
"a comrade-in-arms."

06:41.630 --> 06:44.800
You said that so everyone could hear, right?

06:45.060 --> 06:47.990
Everyone's in love with you now!

06:47.990 --> 06:50.350
Morale's through the roof!

06:50.350 --> 06:54.390
They're all ready to come 
together and fight for you!

06:55.530 --> 06:57.460
I'm so jealous.

06:57.460 --> 07:02.770
I want you to use me as 
a pawn, like you did him.

07:03.180 --> 07:06.360
It's the best way I could be used!

07:06.680 --> 07:10.360
I don't think of my men as pawns.

07:10.360 --> 07:11.620
Right, right.

07:11.950 --> 07:15.620
But if you told me I was a comrade-in-arms,

07:16.110 --> 07:17.830
I might burst out laughing!

07:18.860 --> 07:23.400
You and me and Sergeant. Tsukishima and 
Yuusaku-dono and that rich kid Koito,

07:23.400 --> 07:25.140
we're all pawns!

07:25.460 --> 07:28.960
You're not even worthy of 
<i>trying</i> to oppose Lieutenant Tsurumi!

07:28.960 --> 07:30.740
You're just obsessed with him 
'cause he's the only person

07:30.740 --> 07:32.980
who even pretends to give a shit about you!

07:32.980 --> 07:34.930
I can tell!

07:34.930 --> 07:36.310
I know exactly what you're thinking!

07:36.910 --> 07:38.430
If I were

07:40.000 --> 07:43.590
to play along with your 
feeble-minded delusion...

07:43.950 --> 07:46.060
Even if we're all peasants,

07:46.330 --> 07:49.690
you're the son of a peasant,
and the cheapest pawn of them all.

08:01.960 --> 08:04.900
Are you okay, Private Usami?

08:06.120 --> 08:08.090
He hit me with the bedpan.

08:08.570 --> 08:11.310
Private Mishima is going after him.

08:12.110 --> 08:17.090
Did hear that? He called 
me the cheapest pawn.

08:17.090 --> 08:19.970
No, I didn't.

08:21.020 --> 08:23.120
That can't be right, can it?

08:23.900 --> 08:26.090
Fuck! Fuck!

08:26.820 --> 08:30.460
Ogata Hyakunosuke is going to 
show up again one of these days!

08:31.070 --> 08:34.020
To cause problems for Lieutenant Tsurumi!

08:44.410 --> 08:46.250
<b>Noguchi Hotel</b>

08:48.910 --> 08:51.110
Ogata caught us a duck!

08:51.110 --> 08:53.470
I'm finally used to shooting 
with my left hand.

08:53.740 --> 08:57.970
So our sniper's made a complete recovery?

08:58.180 --> 08:59.410
Nope.

09:00.570 --> 09:04.260
You're not a sniper unless you shoot <i>people</i>.

09:05.660 --> 09:10.070
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

09:12.920 --> 09:16.640
Sugimoto is always close 
to Asirpa-chan, isn't he?

09:16.640 --> 09:19.740
He treasures her 'cause she's a good hunter.

09:20.580 --> 09:24.840
I really don't get why you're 
working with the two of them.

09:24.840 --> 09:28.520
Facing off with lunatics like the 
7th Division and Hijikata Toshizou

09:28.520 --> 09:29.750
is a dangerous business.

09:30.260 --> 09:33.990
You're the kind of man who'd split the 
moment things didn't go your way, right?

09:33.990 --> 09:37.040
Eh, it just kind of ended up that way.

09:37.040 --> 09:40.350
If there's fewer people on your side, 
you don't have to split the money as much.

09:40.980 --> 09:43.830
It's not a sign that you 
really think they can win?

09:47.810 --> 09:53.420
That girl's got the same deep blue 
eyes as Nopperabo, doesn't she?

09:53.420 --> 09:59.210
Nah. I'm told that a lot of Ainu 
have Russian blood, though.

10:00.560 --> 10:03.450
We can't trust each other, sure.

10:03.450 --> 10:06.750
But we can't risk our lives for 
each other unless we share all the

10:07.040 --> 10:08.960
information we've got.

10:11.290 --> 10:18.130
This is just my guess, but I think 
Asirpa-chan already knows how to crack the code.

10:19.200 --> 10:22.340
Did she tell you?

10:23.300 --> 10:23.970
No.

10:26.530 --> 10:27.540
I see.

10:28.900 --> 10:32.200
I'm not that trusted, either.

10:33.460 --> 10:35.080
Look at this, Shiraishi.

10:37.770 --> 10:39.560
What is this?

10:40.230 --> 10:41.490
A gold piece?

10:41.490 --> 10:44.850
It was found alongside the gold dust 
at the bottom of Lake Shikotsu.

10:45.370 --> 10:49.450
Doesn't that mark look like our tattoos?

10:50.740 --> 10:52.330
An atkamuy!

10:52.330 --> 10:55.390
Its round head is so cute! So cute!

10:55.390 --> 10:57.760
Shall we catch it and turn it 
into a pair of gloves for you?

10:57.760 --> 10:59.090
No thanks! No thanks!

10:59.660 --> 11:03.720
Atkamuy are protectors of children.
They help people.

11:03.720 --> 11:05.610
Just like Horkewkamuy.

11:05.990 --> 11:09.360
I found Retar when he 
was a child around here.

11:11.250 --> 11:16.090
That star, the one next to it, and 
the one next to it, make up kunociw,

11:16.090 --> 11:17.190
the Bow constellation.

11:19.250 --> 11:20.690
It looks like a bow!

11:22.390 --> 11:25.200
That's aynociw, the arrow constellation.

11:26.970 --> 11:29.580
Siarasarusikamuynokanociw...

11:29.580 --> 11:32.290
A constellation shaped 
like a long-tailed bear.

11:33.790 --> 11:38.020
So that star, and that one, 
and that one, what do they look like?

11:38.020 --> 11:39.550
Um...

11:41.050 --> 11:42.760
Like a dick!

11:42.760 --> 11:45.380
There probably isn't a dick constellation.

11:45.710 --> 11:48.350
That's the nociw for a Horkewkamuy.

11:48.590 --> 11:51.120
That's the front leg and that's the tail...

11:51.120 --> 11:53.210
What kind of kamuy are the horkew?

11:57.350 --> 11:59.380
Kamuy that vanished.

12:00.840 --> 12:03.110
It was after that when I met Retar,

12:03.110 --> 12:06.290
and learned what a Horkewkamuy looks like.

12:06.820 --> 12:08.490
I hope the next generation of children

12:08.860 --> 12:11.920
get to see what the 
Horkewkamuy looks like, too.

12:12.730 --> 12:15.670
You know, if Retar has a 
lot of kids in this forest.

12:15.670 --> 12:17.360
Right, Asirpa-san?

12:22.020 --> 12:24.760
<i>Aca's name, Horkew Oskoni.</i>

12:25.170 --> 12:28.010
<i>That has to be the clue to breaking the code.</i>

12:28.480 --> 12:32.350
<i>He put the Ainu name my mother 
gave him into the code.</i>

12:32.620 --> 12:37.160
<i>I can't believe someone like that would 
kill so many Ainu and steal the gold.</i>

12:37.910 --> 12:40.900
<i>Is that why Kiroranke Nispa killed Aca?</i>

12:41.680 --> 12:46.530
<i>The gold changed their fates... 
everyone's fate... for the worse.</i>

12:47.020 --> 12:50.200
<i>Is it really best if the gold's found?</i>

12:50.840 --> 12:56.220
<i>If I don't tell Sugimoto how to 
solve the code, he'll stay with me.</i>

12:57.030 --> 12:59.390
<i>I can serve as a bullet shield for him.</i>

13:00.130 --> 13:05.440
<i>Maybe it would be better if we never found 
the gold, and stayed together forever.</i>

13:06.710 --> 13:11.960
Sugimoto, what will you do 
if you do find the gold?

13:18.920 --> 13:22.530
Go back home and live with 
the person you loved?

13:24.600 --> 13:27.020
<i>If the gold is found,</i>

13:28.170 --> 13:29.660
<i>Sugimoto will leave me.</i>

13:32.330 --> 13:33.200
What is that?

13:33.700 --> 13:34.960
Markings?

13:36.580 --> 13:37.650
And on that tree, too!

13:38.710 --> 13:41.940
There are markings on all 
the trees in this area!

13:41.940 --> 13:44.120
We should get out of here now.

13:44.120 --> 13:45.430
Hurry, Sugimoto!

13:56.170 --> 13:57.960
What's going on?

14:17.930 --> 14:20.500
This is how they chop down trees in Hokkaido.

14:20.920 --> 14:25.960
They chop some of them down partially, 
and then knock over the first one.

14:26.300 --> 14:29.220
And then all the others fall one 
after another, like shogi pieces.

14:29.900 --> 14:33.220
The two of them went into this forest!

14:33.220 --> 14:35.770
They didn't get flattened, right?

14:35.770 --> 14:37.450
Sugimoto!

14:37.450 --> 14:38.040
Hey!

14:38.040 --> 14:39.770
Asirpa-chan!

14:41.050 --> 14:42.100
Asirpa-san!

14:44.730 --> 14:45.850
Asirpa-san!

14:48.850 --> 14:51.990
Sugimoto, are you okay?

14:51.990 --> 14:53.850
What about you?

14:53.850 --> 14:54.960
Does it hurt?

14:54.960 --> 14:57.140
Are you stuck at all?

14:57.140 --> 14:58.460
Your arms and legs, maybe?

14:59.690 --> 15:00.860
I don't know...

15:00.860 --> 15:01.740
Wake up!

15:01.740 --> 15:05.000
Stay strong, we're getting out of here!

15:11.080 --> 15:12.930
General Togo!

15:14.070 --> 15:16.600
General Togo is mine once more!

15:18.060 --> 15:20.020
<b>Uemura</b>

15:21.350 --> 15:23.650
You're never getting promoted, Tsukishima!

15:24.010 --> 15:26.080
You're telling me to let you win at menko?

15:27.180 --> 15:31.620
Also, Lieutenant Tsurumi wants 
us to wait at Sapporo.

15:32.040 --> 15:34.850
He's giving up the search 
for Asirpa and heading—

15:45.130 --> 15:46.460
Someone you know?

15:47.070 --> 15:51.590
No. But she seems quite 
dangerous. Be careful.

16:00.140 --> 16:02.240
<i>I need to control myself for now...</i>

16:03.250 --> 16:06.190
<i>To find Asirpa!</i>

16:06.810 --> 16:09.780
Is anyone here? Shiraishi!

16:13.780 --> 16:17.340
Are you going back home to 
live with the person you love?

16:18.570 --> 16:21.030
There's this girl called Ume-chan.

16:22.900 --> 16:26.710
I was supposed to marry her.

16:29.010 --> 16:33.910
But after my whole family died 
from tuberculosis, that never happened.

16:39.590 --> 16:41.790
She married Toraji.

16:48.400 --> 16:50.750
He was her childhood friend, too,

16:51.110 --> 16:54.150
and I knew that he'd take good care of her.

16:54.840 --> 16:59.490
But she got an eye disease 
that would cost a lot to cure.

17:06.310 --> 17:07.500
And Toraji...

17:16.970 --> 17:23.950
If I told her I threw you... 
would Umeko believe it?

17:29.590 --> 17:33.480
Sugimoto! Asirpa-chan!

17:35.200 --> 17:39.660
Sugimoto! Asirpa-chan!

17:39.660 --> 17:42.390
If you're that worried about them,

17:42.390 --> 17:45.350
then the girl must be the key, right?

17:45.700 --> 17:48.100
She's Nopperabo's daughter, right?

17:48.100 --> 17:49.830
Well, Shiraishi?

17:49.830 --> 17:51.370
Shut up!

17:51.370 --> 17:54.300
Who gives a shit either way?

17:55.320 --> 18:01.320
I have to keep my promise and go home 
to give her the money she needs.

18:02.890 --> 18:06.520
I'm glad the reason you want the gold is 
one that sounds like the Sugimoto I know.

18:07.130 --> 18:10.540
Then you need the gold no matter what, right?

18:11.060 --> 18:12.860
Even if we do find the gold,

18:13.460 --> 18:19.160
I'll stay your partner until you're 
satisfied with how things have turned out.

18:21.910 --> 18:25.920
That wasn't the answer I really wanted...

18:27.220 --> 18:29.460
But first, let's get out of here.

18:29.720 --> 18:32.120
The others are sure to come and save us.

18:32.460 --> 18:34.210
They might have gotten trapped themselves.

18:34.430 --> 18:38.930
Still, they'll come searching 
for us no matter what.

18:38.930 --> 18:44.110
Shiraishi wants the gold really bad,
 in a different way than you.

18:44.690 --> 18:46.680
He's incredibly greedy.

18:47.580 --> 18:51.870
Yeah, but he kept his promise with me.

18:51.870 --> 18:54.890
He stayed by you the whole time in Karafuto.

18:57.630 --> 19:01.320
So wouldn't it be okay to 
tell him, like you did me,

19:02.080 --> 19:06.120
that you remembered the key to the code?

19:06.350 --> 19:07.100
Yeah.

19:07.420 --> 19:13.820
I could've said it earlier, 
but I kind of missed my chance.

19:15.690 --> 19:17.720
The atkamuy came to save us!

19:18.650 --> 19:22.930
I'm so glad all that happened 
in Karafuto wasn't for nothing!

19:22.930 --> 19:24.630
Shiraishi!

19:24.630 --> 19:27.100
I can't believe you found us.

19:27.530 --> 19:29.910
Mister Hood saw it!

19:30.660 --> 19:32.300
Hey, help us!

19:32.300 --> 19:35.400
My comrades are trapped 
under the trees you felled!

19:35.400 --> 19:36.810
Oh, no!

19:37.300 --> 19:38.350
Where are they?

19:53.100 --> 19:56.630
Where did the kamuy here go, you think?

19:58.890 --> 20:02.730
So the forest looked like this on this side?

20:02.730 --> 20:04.410
I didn't realize.

20:04.950 --> 20:07.590
We cut trees, too.

20:08.070 --> 20:13.480
Just like the Japanese, we kill deer, bear, 
even wolves, and sell their pelts.

20:13.980 --> 20:17.980
Nobody can blame you for 
wanting to live a good life.

20:19.010 --> 20:21.190
You just need to not take too much.

20:21.740 --> 20:26.700
When we hunt, we don't take all the meat. 
We leave a little for the mountain.

20:27.400 --> 20:29.070
We leave some herbs, too.

20:29.410 --> 20:31.410
Because there'll be more next year...

20:32.010 --> 20:34.420
That's always what we've done.

20:35.010 --> 20:39.230
If we leave a little behind instead of 
taking everything, our kamuy won't vanish.

20:40.220 --> 20:42.130
I remember that's what Aca said.

20:42.960 --> 20:47.650
Botaro, why don't you show 
Asirpa-chan that gold piece?

20:48.150 --> 20:50.430
She's Nopperabo's daughter.

20:50.430 --> 20:51.980
Hey, Shiraishi.

20:51.980 --> 20:55.480
Don't worry. He figured 
it out a long time ago.

20:56.250 --> 20:58.670
This was at the bottom of Lake Shikotsu.

20:58.670 --> 21:00.230
You take it.

21:00.500 --> 21:06.240
That pattern looks like our tattoos.
 Wilk must've made this.

21:06.820 --> 21:10.370
This looks like Ainu.

21:10.750 --> 21:14.120
It means "in turn" or "crossing paths."

21:14.470 --> 21:20.650
I wonder if the Ainu from long ago brought 
all their gold together in one place,

21:21.110 --> 21:25.730
then melted down a part of it to celebrate 
their dream of having their own nation.

21:27.140 --> 21:31.790
Aca once told Sofia in Russia that the 
Ainu and other Far Eastern minorities

21:31.790 --> 21:33.530
should come together.

21:34.640 --> 21:38.740
If he held this with him until 
the day it sank into Lake Shikotsu,

21:39.090 --> 21:41.690
it means his desire for us all to come 
together and protect what we have

21:41.690 --> 21:43.530
never changed.

21:44.330 --> 21:47.850
He would never try to kill the 
people he was going to save.

21:49.810 --> 21:51.900
Aca didn't kill those Ainu.

21:55.860 --> 22:01.370
And I've finally realized what 
it is I have to do for the Ainu.

23:35.200 --> 23:40.250
<b>Anime Final Chapter Production Greenlit!!</b>
